const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"验证成本：交易属性能否被可信确认",en:"Verification costs concern establishing transaction attributes"},body:{zh:"Catalini与Gans从交易双方需要确认的属性出发，例如所有权、资金是否存在以及交易是否履行。可信验证可能依赖中介，也可能依赖共享记录。框架关心的是这种验证成本如何变化，不是简单比较账本写入速度或交易手续费。",en:"The framework starts with attributes parties must verify, such as ownership, available funds and performance. Verification may rely on intermediaries or shared records. The economic question concerns changing verification costs, not merely ledger throughput or transaction fees."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §2",en:"June 2019 revision · §2"}}},{title:{zh:"网络成本：怎样建立并维持共同基础设施",en:"Networking costs concern building and sustaining shared infrastructure"},body:{zh:"第二类成本涉及如何启动和维持一个网络，而不仅是连接电脑。协议规则与经济激励可以协调为基础设施贡献资源的参与者。能验证一笔记录，并不自动解决参与者为何加入、谁承担运行成本或网络怎样持续获得维护这些问题。",en:"Networking concerns bootstrapping and operating a marketplace, not just connecting computers. Rules and incentives coordinate contributors to shared infrastructure. Verifying a record does not itself explain why participants join, who pays operating costs or how maintenance continues."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §3",en:"June 2019 revision · §3"}}},{title:{zh:"原生数字状态与线下资产映射不同",en:"Native digital state differs from representations of offline assets"},body:{zh:"原生链上资产的状态可以由系统规则直接检验，但一件线下商品是否存在、品质如何，仍需可信输入。把商品编号写到链上，只保存了关于商品的声明。后续记录难以篡改，不会追溯性地让最初错误或虚假的输入变成真实。",en:"A native digital asset's state can be checked within system rules, while an offline product's existence or quality needs trustworthy input. Recording an identifier preserves a claim about the product. Making later alteration difficult does not make an initially false claim true."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §2 · p. 12",en:"June 2019 revision · §2 · p. 12"}}},{title:{zh:"中介的工作可能改变，而不是全部消失",en:"Intermediaries may change roles rather than disappear"},body:{zh:"论文认为技术更可能改变中介如何创造价值和拥有市场力量，而非消除所有中介。身份、争议处理与链外事件仍可能需要其他机构。评估一个应用时，应列出哪些信任被协议替代、哪些仍由参与者或外部服务承担。",en:"The paper argues that technology can change intermediaries' value creation and market power rather than remove them all. Identity, disputes and offline events may still require institutions. Evaluate which trust relationships the protocol replaces and which remain elsewhere."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §1; §2 · pp. 4, 12–13",en:"June 2019 revision · §1; §2 · pp. 4, 12–13"}}},{title:{zh:"分散验证不保证每笔交易更便宜",en:"Decentralized verification need not be cheaper per transaction"},body:{zh:"作者明确区分单笔处理效率与竞争、控制权、隐私和单点故障等潜在收益。即使去中心化处理比集中处理消耗更多资源，也可能在其他维度提供价值；反过来，不能只因贴上去中心化标签，就推断所有成本都下降。",en:"The paper separates per-transaction efficiency from potential benefits in competition, control, privacy and single points of failure. Decentralized processing can consume more resources while offering other value. The decentralized label alone does not establish that every cost falls."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §2 · pp. 12–13",en:"June 2019 revision · §2 · pp. 12–13"}}},{title:{zh:"先找适用条件，再讨论采用价值",en:"Identify suitable conditions before claiming adoption value"},body:{zh:"结论把链外连接难度、网络利益分配、新数字权利和隐私需求列为判断条件。若这些条件不成立，传统中介与关系合同可能仍然合适。技术能协调一套规则，不等于某个项目已经解决治理、欺诈或用户采用问题，也不是购买代币的理由。",en:"The conclusion emphasizes offline-link frictions, allocation of network benefits, digital rights and privacy needs. Traditional intermediaries can remain suitable when those conditions fail. Coordinating rules does not establish that a project has solved governance, fraud or adoption, nor justify purchasing its token."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22952/w22952.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年6月修订稿 · §4 · p. 23",en:"June 2019 revision · §4 · p. 23"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是关于验证和网络组织成本的经济框架，不是代币估值或协议安全证明。链上记录一致不保证链外事实真实；去中心化的收益与成本取决于具体场景。",en:"This is an economic framework for verification and network organization, not token valuation or a security proof. Consistent records do not guarantee truthful offline facts; costs and benefits depend on context."}};export{e as default};
